WEBVTT

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.350
Orine!

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.020
Here it comes!

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.410
<i>Sakura.</i>

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.370
<i>How come?</i>

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.500
<i>I know the sakura haven't bloomed yet,</i>

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.960
<i>but I still came back.</i>

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:23.670
<i>So why?</i>

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.460
Orine!

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.130
Nagisa!

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:34.970
Are you okay?

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.140
Y-Yeah.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:36.930
Let's get out of here!

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.050
Okay!

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:52.610
This way!

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.240
Hurry!

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.070
Orine.

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:57.570
All right.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:59.410
Come and get me!

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.590
I can't believe I was building weapons...

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:13.590
to destroy the 00 I loved.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.300
But you didn't know!

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.220
I'm the one you should be blaming.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.060
Huh?

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:31.070
It was my father's company that made you create weapons.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.230
But... that's not your fault, Chieri!

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:35.610
And it's not <i>your</i> fault, either!

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:37.740
Chieri...

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.040
Chieri?

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.540
I'm sorry, Orine.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.500
You just stay where you are.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.380
<i>I'll</i> defeat it for you!

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.630
Chieri!

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.350
<i>Can I let it simply end here?</i>

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.270
<i>There's no way I'm going to lose...</i>

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.390
<i>just yet!</i>

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.280
Chieri!

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.700
Now, while it's distracted!

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:26.500
Coming!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.500
There's a car by the back gate.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.920
Get to it quickly.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.540
We're gathering the others.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.000
Thank you so much.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.800
Come on, Orine.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.010
Sakura...

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.350
Orine! Chieri!

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.060
Nagisa!

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.190
Thank goodness.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.770
Come, this way.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.230
We'll rush you to the <i>Flying Get</i> at once.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.360
I'm going to rescue my father!

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.070
But... we can't put you in danger...

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.530
But it's my fault that Daddy is—

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.200
Nagisa, I'm with you.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.040
Kanata-san.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.910
No. We can't jeopardize the concert.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.170
We've all been trained for combat

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.800
so that we can protect those
who love entertainment.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.340
We're going in, girls!

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.220
Roger!

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.380
Ow...

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.800
Hold on.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.430
Kanata-san...

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.680
You really <i>are</i> your father's daughter.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.560
You knew my father?

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.890
Yes.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.860
Your father was a hero to us of the liberation movement.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.280
Daddy was <i>that</i> awesome?

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.110
Yes, he was. Like you wouldn't believe.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.530
Change of plans!

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:49.700
We're gonna help these girls rescue Nagisa-san's father!

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.330
Got it?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.540
Yes, sir!

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:07.310
<i>That day, we ran through this tunnel with our hearts racing.</i>

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:11.810
<i>And then, we heard the voice that signaled the start of the concert...</i>

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:14.520
AKB0048!

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:27.740
But this is where our dreams were born...

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.580
There's the entrance to the detainment facility.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:35.080
The pro-entertainment faction is being held underground.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:39.460
There's a route to the facility's underground in these mines.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:44.010
We'll start attacking from out here to draw the attention of the lookouts.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:49.470
While they're occupied, you'll infiltrate from below.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.470
So we're using diversionary tactics?

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.770
I'll go with the WOTA.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:54.230
Yuuka!

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.650
It's too dangerous. You can't come.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:00.530
But you're—<i>everyone</i> is doing their part.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:06.990
I want to help Nagisa—to help our home planet!

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.120
Yuuka...

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.950
I'll come with you.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.540
Kanata-san.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.830
Nagisa. Rescue your father at all costs.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.500
Of course!

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:55.250
There's more of them than usual.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:59.210
They must be on guard because of the concert.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.840
Mamoru, what's wrong?

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.180
Why are you putting yourself in danger?

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.720
What if you get hurt?

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.640
You're an idol.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.220
Everyone is waiting for you.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.980
Remember the position you're in—

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.900
We're on a mission.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.230
<i>You</i> remember <i>your</i> position.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.270
I get it...

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:28.570
Roger.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.320
They're at the entry point.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.000
Is that 00?

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.040
This way!

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.550
It's to the left of here.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.880
To the left! To the left!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.050
Sonata!

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:02.310
Megu!

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:13.740
Daddy?

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.030
Daddy!

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.410
Nagisa?

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.500
What are you doing here?

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.710
Thank goodness! I'll get you right out.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:22.670
This is dangerous, so stand back.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.130
Stop that, Nagisa.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.630
I have no intention of leaving this place.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.470
I will speak to the higher-ups myself.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.510
Why? I mean—

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:37.220
I am an Entertainment Administration official.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:44.770
I can't afford to be sprung from prison by an entertainer and traitor to Lancastar.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:46.650
Daddy...

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.650
Can everyone hear me?

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.110
Yes!

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.110
They know you're in there.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:52.860
Fall back!

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.120
Get him out, quick!

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.030
N-Nagisa...

00:07:58.740 --> 00:07:59.830
Nagisa-san.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.040
Just go!

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.420
Daddy...

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:06.790
Daddy.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:10.510
Daddy!

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.470
Four more bowls of rice.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.100
And one extra-large!

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:22.690
Got it!

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:24.770
You have some too, Yuuka.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:25.730
Have some!

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:28.320
I know, I'll have some later.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.690
Come on, you've got food on your face.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.490
Here's your order!

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:39.410
Yuuka-san's parents are
always so kind to us WOTA.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:41.410
Free refills on rice!

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.370
Free pork in the miso soup!

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.460
You were lucky.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:50.050
The shielding on your uniform minimized the damage.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:54.340
But... now I can't go on stage.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.890
This was my chance to be with Youko.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:01.060
There's always next time.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:06.770
Sheesh, you should have said <i>something.</i>

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:10.190
Your e-mails mentioned nothing about Lancastar.

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:14.110
We thought you'd worry if you knew.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.950
Mr. and Mrs. Ichijou!

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.410
Please, tell me.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.830
Is it my fault that Daddy is in the detainment facility?

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:35.090
Well, we managed to lie our way out of it...

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:41.350
Your father was pressured to make you quit 00.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:46.060
But Motomiya-san would hear nothing of it.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.820
We're about to pass your house.

00:09:58.410 --> 00:09:59.530
Yeah...

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.280
Do you want to see your mother?

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.540
It's okay.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:08.750
If I visited her, I'd just cause trouble.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.710
Mommy...

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:18.260
But she took such good care of them!

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:26.680
<i>The smoke from the factories is dulling their color.</i>

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:29.190
<i>Why don't you buy flowers that are easier to grow?</i>

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:32.690
<i>The more effort they take to raise, the more you love them.</i>

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:33.900
<i>Just like you.</i>

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.160
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.030
<i>It's all my fault.</i>

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.530
<i>Both Daddy and you...</i>

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.580
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:52.500
Take Megumi to the sick bay.

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.340
The rest of you, start practicing!

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.550
We're running out of time.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.170
Start with "Seaside Cherry"!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:10:59.590
Okay!

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:27.950
Nagisa?

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.080
Nagisa, what's wrong?

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:44.510
It's probably a psychological issue.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:48.180
Sometimes people lose their voice when they're under a lot of stress.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:49.680
Oh dear.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.520
The concert is tomorrow. We don't have time.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:57.020
Other members can take over
Nagisa's part for most of the songs.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.570
But the problem is "Seaside Cherry".

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:01.990
We'll have to change the set list—

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.780
Please, let me sing it!

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:06.580
Chieri...

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.790
I've been practicing with her.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:13.580
I know the lyrics and choreography by heart.

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:15.170
Chieri, are you sure?

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.210
Yes. Please let me do it.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:21.380
Very well.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:25.390
Nagisa, you're now a backup dancer.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.060
As for Nagisa's part in the other songs...

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:29.100
I can handle it.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:30.310
Me too.

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.980
Nagisa, don't worry.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.060
We'll take care of it.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:10.220
Honestly, I don't see what's so great about this song.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.270
Yuuko...

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.310
I hate this song.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:18.310
All this "to the next generation" business.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:21.360
Does that mean <i>our</i> generation isn't good enough?

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:22.820
It's like we're being jeered at.

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:26.860
Takamina!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.120
Are you okay?

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:31.620
You're burning up!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:34.660
I'm fine.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.870
Just my old injuries acting up.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.040
<i>No!</i>

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.510
Why didn't you say anything?

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:45.050
I'm fine.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:47.890
I'm on medication for the pain.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:48.800
Besides...

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:54.430
I'm thinking of graduating from 00 after this concert.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:00.400
I'll pass my dreams to the next generation.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.820
They'll be Kanata's to pursue.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:08.110
Takamina...

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:11.700
That's not right!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.750
Yuuka, how many times do I have to say it?

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.000
You must master Nagisa's part!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:17.750
I'm sorry!

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.710
You too, Orine! Sing louder!

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:23.380
You need enough volume for both your parts!

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.340
Right!

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:30.090
<i>I've caused trouble for everyone because I can't sing.</i>

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:34.100
<i>Daddy and Mommy are suffering.</i>

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.850
<i>It's all my fault.</i>

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.310
They just might pull it off.

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.610
Well, barely.

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.900
Good work, girls.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:48.320
We don't have much time until the performance, but take a break.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.200
Okay.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.070
Thank you very much!

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.920
Are you looking for Tsubasa-san?

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:13.680
Nagisa. Don't tell me you're trying to graduate from 00.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:20.810
Didn't you tell me 00 wasn't about winning or losing?

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:24.900
If you ask me, though, that's not the case.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.070
That just sounds like an excuse.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:31.950
Like you're averting your gaze from your own potential.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.080
That's what I think.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:41.330
If you want to graduate, I won't stop you.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.000
But I have a request.

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:48.420
If you're going to graduate from 00,

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:52.430
do it <i>after</i> you've danced
"Seaside Cherry" behind me.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:55.890
Don't quit until you've lost to me.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:07.770
We're about to start the understudy performance.

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.530
I want everyone to give their all at this concert.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.820
Don't hold back a thing!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:14.030
Okay!

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:17.240
To the WOTA members,

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:21.500
your strength will give these girls courage.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.000
We are honored to have your service.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:23.670
Yeah!

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:24.330
You bet!

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.580
Let's do this!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:31.340
Now, along with the preparations for the concert, let us review our defensive strategies.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:35.510
First, concerning the starting time and location...

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:44.650
Mamoru!

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:45.270
Yuuka.

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:46.810
What's up?

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.980
Thank you, Mamoru.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:56.870
I know it won't be easy, but I'll
put on a dazzling performance!

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.950
Right. Go get 'em.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:00.830
I'm looking forward to it.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:09.840
It feels like I'm in a dream.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:12.760
You're now a WOTA,

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:17.550
even though you said you wouldn't love me once I became a 00 idol.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.680
I've changed my mind.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:27.440
I love Yuuka the 00 member.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.990
Mamoru...

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:39.660
However, I no longer love the Yuuka who isn't in 00.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.370
So I'll always be cheering for you.

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:50.040
As long as you're in 00, I'll be your fan.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.800
Mamoru!

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:56.680
It's time to assemble.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:57.840
You're late!

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:58.640
Coming!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:01.010
Well, break a leg.

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:03.890
We'll be there to make sure the stage is safe.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:08.060
What are you doing? The others are waiting.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.610
Sorry, sorry.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.360
Yuuka-san.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:17.950
Where were you?

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:19.910
Sorry about that.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.910
Okay! Huddle time!

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.370
Ready, set...

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:30.000
Always thankful, calm, kind, and just!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.710
Smiles and happiness for all!

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.800
<i>Smiles for all...</i>

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.300
<i>That's right.</i>

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.760
Here we go!

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:44.720
AKB0048!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:02.820
It's starting.

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:06.160
Good evening, everyone!

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.620
Good evening!

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:08.960
It's nice to meet you!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:13.630
We're the AKB0048 understudies!

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:18.470
Chieri-chan!

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:32.440
Today is the first understudy performance.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:40.570
We're nervous, but we want you to enjoy entertainment and 00 to the fullest!

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.070
Listen to our song.

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:45.240
"Shout-out Diamond"!

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:04.640
The bus sets off, and I chase after.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:07.430
I want you to know

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:10.140
how I feel.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:15.440
The uncertainty is gone from my heart.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:20.940
I know what's important now.

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:25.660
<i>Mamoru and the others are
protecting our performance.</i>

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:22.950
Though the answer

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:26.370
is right before my eyes,

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:32.250
what held me back as I saw you off?

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:37.250
To make sure I don't lose myself,

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.830
Damn you, WOTA!

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:38.170
Pew-pew!

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:44.050
I'll listen to my instincts.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:38.920
Holy cow!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.220
I love you, I love you so much.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:50.430
I'll chase you with all my might.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.680
I love you, I'll always love you.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:56.310
I'll shout at the top of my lungs.

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:58.360
I love you, I love you so much

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.570
My breath catches in my throat.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:04.400
I can't hold it in,

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:09.240
this shout-out diamond.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.280
Curses. They're serious this time.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:12.200
I love you, I love you so much.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:15.330
I'll chase you with all my might.

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:17.630
I love you, I'll always love you.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:20.880
I'll shout at the top of my lungs.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:26.300
<i>I'm sure, to me... you'll always be...</i>

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.050
I love you, I love you so much

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:26.260
May that love reach you.

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:28.640
I love you, I'll always love you.

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:31.930
I'll shout out to the wind.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:29.930
<i>These feelings...</i>

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:33.390
<i>...will always</i>

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:37.520
My breath catches in my throat.

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:36.060
<i>remain in my heart.</i>

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:37.560
All hands! Emergency retreat!

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:39.980
The concert is canceled!

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:40.230
No way!

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:45.860
this shout-out diamond.

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:45.860
I'll gather my courage and say it.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:48.490
If I bottle it up, nothing will change.

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.820
<i>Farewell, Mamoru.</i>

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.490
There's nothing to be embarrassed about.

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:50.580
Orine?

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:54.160
There's nothing like the words, "I love you."

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:56.870
There's nothing like the words, "I love you."

00:21:56.870 --> 00:22:02.590
There's nothing like the words, "I love you."

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.090
A new Kirara.

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:05.050
We'll return someday!

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:07.970
Let out all my emotions

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:10.430
so I can be true to myself.

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:47.730
Go on, let your feelings reach out

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:49.360
to all the people of Lancastar!

00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:51.110
We're going in!

00:23:51.110 --> 00:23:52.770
The party's about to start!

00:23:52.770 --> 00:23:54.620
<i>Come. Let's begin.</i>

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:57.460
<i>Our sweat and tears will bring about</i>

00:23:57.460 --> 00:24:00.040
<i>a brand new dream.</i>

00:23:57.790 --> 00:24:00.040
- For Their Smiles-
